00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:00.900
The invention.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.060
Of polyurethane skateboard wheels in the
early.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.900
1970s suddenly made jumps and tight cornering
possible.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.750
Because these wheels had a better grip.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:10.290
On riding.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.660
Surfaces than the old metal or ceramic
wheels.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.640
They were more durable and the shock
absorption was greatly improved.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.440
Skateboard wheels come in different sizes
hardness, colors and graphic.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.340
Designs.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.370
For the rider.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.370
There are many practical and aesthetic
considerations.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.340
Making skateboard wheels starts with a
computer design.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.100
They'll use the software to guide cutting
tools.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.910
The tools carve into a solid.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:46.290
Aluminum puck and transform it into one half
of a wheel mold.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:50.560
Next.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.990
The other half of the mold takes shape as the
computerized tooling sculpts another puck to

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.940
a profile that fits to the first one
perfectly.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.750
Not all of the skateboard wheel molds are
two part versions.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.180
Others are one piece structures.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.600
Each with a pin in the center to form a
bearing cavity.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.930
A nozzle dispenses freshly mixed
polyurethane liquid into the wheel molds.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.680
The liquid starts to solidify immediately.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.150
To complete the process, they load the.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:31.530
Polyurethane filled molds into an oven and
bake them at 115.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:32.550
Degrees Celsius.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.870
For 40 minutes.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.940
During baking any bubbles.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.460
In the polyurethane rise to the top and are
diffused.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.230
Leaving solid.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.390
Forms with no weak spots.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.560
Workers remove the pins from the molds.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.110
Then it's on to the next station.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:01.530
Here, a worker blasts compressed air between
the wheels and the molds to pry the wheels.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.150
Free and pop them out.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.220
A worker bounces one of the wheels.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.150
To demonstrate.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:09.720
Its high.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.590
Rebound.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:16.050
It's an indication that the skateboard wheel
will roll easily with very little drag.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:21.960
He probes the wheel using a barometer gauge
to ensure the urethane has cured to the

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.250
proper hardness.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.260
If the sample wheel is sufficiently hard,
the batch is.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.700
Ready for the next step.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.640
The worker clamps the skateboard wheel in a
lathe.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:39.180
The lathe spins the wheel while an automatic
cutter contours the edges to a softer, more

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.410
rounded profile.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.750
To give the skateboard wheels visual impact.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.510
An artist selects and arranges graphic.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.070
Designs on a computer.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:52.680
He prints a.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.350
Film negative of the images he's chosen.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.100
They'll use this negative to produce a.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.810
Printing plate from a piece of metal that's
been coated with a light sensitive substance

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.280
known as emulsion.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:06.780
He places the.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.790
Film negative on the plate inside a.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.080
Uv light chamber.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.140
He closes the lid and activates the UV
light.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:19.080
This triggers a photochemical reaction that
transfers the image from the negative to the

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.660
plate. You can see.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.530
The image now.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:23.130
Exposed.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.290
Very faintly on the printing plate.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:28.590
He applies a solution that.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:29.250
Removes.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.320
Unexposed emulsion and in the.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.240
Process etches the image.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.620
Into the printing plate.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.790
He rinses off the chemicals.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.510
He drives the plate to reveal the etched
artwork.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:48.580
A worker.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.740
Positions a magnetized ink cup.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.850
Over the image.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.700
And installs them in a pad printing machine.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:03.210
The operator loads skateboard wheels onto
posts that index them forward for printing.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.660
The ink cup deposits ink on the printing
plate.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.210
A silicone pad picks up the inked image and
stamps it onto.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.440
The skateboard wheel.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.270
The operator removes the printed wheel and
sets it on a tray.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:23.940
A technician now.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:28.380
Clamps one of the wheels in a testing device
which will gauge the rebound.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.850
He drops a metal.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.980
Ball onto the wheel and measures.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.770
How high it bounces or rebounds.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.270
Again, a high.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.200
Rebound is.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.040
Desirable. The skateboard wheels are.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.510
Now cleared for shipping.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.500
They wrap them in plastic and heat.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.940
Shrink it. It has taken about.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:53.490
Three days to make the skateboard wheels.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:05:00.060
How long they'll last depends a lot on the
rider and how he or she rolls.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:07.970
The annual apple harvest.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:09.530
Is just two months long.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.370
To keep apples.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.380
Fresh in storage for several months.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.760
Growers lower the.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.180
Store room oxygen level to put the apples
into hibernation.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.950
Then they use machines called.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:23.240
Co two scrubbers to absorb and remove the
carbon dioxide gas.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.710
The apples give off.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:30.550
This CO two scrubber pulls air from the
airtight apple storage.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.440
Room through carbon pellets.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.200
Which absorb the CO two gas molecules.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.370
The machine then.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.740
Blows the CO two free air back.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.740
Into the room. Workers build the machines
frame.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.960
Out of tubular steel.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:45.250
The frame supports.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.170
All the components, including two.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:50.020
Sealed vessels filled with carbon pellets.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:54.370
The first vessel starts absorbing CO two, a
process called.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.540
Scrubbing until.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.490
Its pellets are saturated, at.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.170
Which point the second vessel.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:05:59.440
Takes.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.490
Over the scrubbing.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.400
The first vessel automatically kicks into.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.840
A regeneration cycle.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.330
Which blows fresh air through the pellets to
remove.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:13.000
The CO two molecules and exhaust them out the
building when the second vessel's pellets

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:13.420
max.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:13.810
Out.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.210
Vessel one resumes scrubbing.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.500
While vessel two.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.870
Regenerates to construct.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:24.370
Each vessel. Workers weld a steel sheet into
a circular shape.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.800
Then weld on a base and a top ring.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.800
The ring has holes around its perimeter for.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:31.060
Bolting on a lid.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.320
They use.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:36.280
A ring template to make corresponding holes
in the lid, marking.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.320
The exact center of each hole with.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:43.760
A punch tool. They mount the lid on a
fixture, and following.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:44.690
Those marks.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.880
Use an automated steel punch.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.440
To perforate the steel.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.020
The vessels go to the paint booth for a coat
of powder.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.080
Paint then into an oven to bake the paint.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:02.610
When they come out.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.230
They're ready to be filled with.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.240
Carbon pellets and sealed.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.350
Once each vessel is filled to the top,
workers.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:13.880
Lay in a.

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:14.990
Steel baffle.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.070
Its holes evenly distribute air passing
through the vessel.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.070
They place a foam rubber.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.870
Gasket around the perimeter.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.600
And bolt on the lid tightly.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.120
This seals the vessel.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:36.430
Preventing the air being blown through it
from leaking out and preventing oxygen from

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.650
getting into the machine and from there.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:40.420
Into the Appel storage room.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:43.750
Next, they install the PVC.

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:44.740
Piping that.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.740
Feeds air through the vessels, along with two
